WEBVTT

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:20.660
Honda Family

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.660
Hey, Pop. I'm back from Taiwan.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.730
The Taiwanese league was just as intense 
as the Japanese league and the majors.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:30.170
I guess you can find baseball lovers 
in every corner of the world.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.050
Honda Family

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.680
Yeah, I know.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.060
I'll follow your example.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:46.000
I'll try to be a dependable father,
just like you were.

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:20.590
The three major sets of reforms during 
the Edo period were the Kyouho reforms,

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:23.530
The Promise

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:23.530
the Kansei reforms and the Tenpo reforms.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:24.890
Good job!

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:26.160
Let's start out slowly.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.960
I <i>said</i> I got it!

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:33.610
The Kyouho reforms were instituted
by Tokugawa Yoshimune.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.250
Pop, stop holding back!

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.230
You sure?

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.970
Yeah. Just bring it.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.970
The Kansei reforms, by Matsudaira Sadanobu.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.210
The Tenpo reforms, by Mizuno Tadakuni.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.470
Nice catch!

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:47.930
You're catching these 
pitches pretty easily, Izumi.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:50.060
Stop making fun of me!

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.180
Man, a pro's pitches sure do pack a punch...

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:54.020
What's that?

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.710
Oh, nothing.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:57.840
It's coming back.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:58.650
Okay.

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:01.990
You guys are so loud. 
It's still morning, y'know.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.580
I'm trying to study for my entrance exam,
so could you knock it off?

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.620
Oh, you're up, Daigo!

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.790
Grab your glove and get out here.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:11.180
Let's all play together.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.040
Didn't you hear what I just said?

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:17.030
I'm studying for my entrance exams!

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.220
Exams? You're trying to 
get into a private school?

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:25.010
You <i>never</i> study. What's gotten 
into you, all of a sudden?

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.580
Just come down and play catch with us.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.600
Pop just got back yesterday
after being away for so long.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.730
Toshiya's been teaching you 
how to catch, hasn't he?

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:35.900
I wanna see what you've got!

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:40.520
Remember what I promised you
before you joined the Dolphins?

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.530
That I'd play catch with you when I got back?

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.100
No way.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.010
I'm done with baseball.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:49.750
Huh?

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:51.640
You're wasting your time, Pop.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.500
He's been like this since forever.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:56.160
Didn't you hear what happened to Hikaru-kun?

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:00.180
No, I heard about it, all right.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.700
It looks like he's completely 
given up on baseball.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.230
I see.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:13.120
After rejoining the Dolphins, 
he started training real hard.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.010
After meeting Hikaru-kun,

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:17.520
and after learning about 
the catcher position...

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:19.740
Before, he'd lost all 
motivation to do anything,

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:22.110
but after all that, he was 
pumped up every single day.

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:28.870
I really don't like the idea of him 
quitting baseball like this,

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:33.560
but if playing is such 
a painful experience for him,

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.630
I think we should just 
let him do what he wants.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:42.880
Lately, we've even avoided 
<i>talking</i> about baseball around him.

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:46.890
But that feels kinda wrong, too...

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.720
Honestly, I have no idea what to do.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:53.390
It's not a problem.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.400
You haven't done anything wrong.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:03.180
I'm sorry I left you to 
handle this all by yourself.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:08.390
I need some water.

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:19.840
Do you think you could let me sort Daigo out?

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:23.550
Sure.

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:31.830
Games, huh?

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.330
Hey, Pop...

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:37.450
Hey! You're doin' great!

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:39.720
Yeah, just like that! Get 'em, son!

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:42.880
Knock it off! You're distracting me!

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.280
That was close!

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:47.110
Try again.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:55.340
Hey, Daigo!

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:58.380
They've got a manga corner over here.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.030
What kinda stuff are you into?

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.280
I'm buying.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.590
Just pick out one you like.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.590
You're seriously suggesting manga to 
a kid studying for entrance exams?

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.040
Hold up.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:12.600
Hey, Daigo!

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:14.660
You haven't had lunch yet, right?

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.100
I'm not hungry.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:25.790
Eat up! You're a growing lad.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:30.020
So what's the deal with that girl you were 
with the other day? You two going out?

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:33.210
You mean Sakura?!

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:34.440
Of course not!

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:35.850
No?

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:37.790
You looked pretty close from what I saw.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.190
We just happen to walk home
in the same direction!

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:42.380
She's just one of my Dolphins' teammates!

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:46.670
So you have friends on the team, huh?

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.710
Anyway, why are you following me around?

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:53.430
Huh?

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.370
I know what you're doing.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:59.050
Your end goal is to get me to 
take up baseball again, isn't it?

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:02.150
That's not cool, man.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.910
I wouldn't do that to you.

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:06.780
If you don't want to play, 
nobody's gonna force you.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:11.920
I just haven't seen you in such a long time.
I figured we should hang out together.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:15.410
Whatever you want us to do, I'm on board.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.720
Wanna go play soccer? How about karaoke?

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:20.440
C'mon, you can tell me.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:27.190
So what you're saying is that you 
want to study? That right, Daigo-kun?

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:29.950
I can't spend all day playing when 
my entrance exams are coming up.

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:31.890
You don't have to be here, 
if you don't want to.

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:36.080
I passed all my academic 
tests to get into Kaidou.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.970
I'll teach you whatever you want!

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:39.980
Then, how about helping 
me with this one?

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:41.850
Yeah! You got it!

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:47.270
Triangle ABC has side BC divided 
into three sections, at points D and E,

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:51.320
and side AC divided into four 
sections at points F, G, and H.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:59.330
What multiple of the surface area of 
triangle CEH does triangle BFD have?

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:04.650
Like I keep telling you, 
<i>this</i> and<i> this</i> are the same size!

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.500
Which means this bit becomes 2:1.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:09.260
Oh! 2:1, huh?

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:11.180
So there's a chance to make a comeback!

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:12.090
Well?

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:13.790
Just forget it!

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:15.590
I'll do it myself!

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.310
You serious?

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:21.270
Yup! Dead serious!

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:24.990
I went up to bat, knowing that this 
was our chance to turn the tables,

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:27.200
but the bat flew clean out of my hands.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:30.140
All of their infielders just scattered!

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.240
You're as energetic as ever, Shigeno.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.780
So true.

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:39.830
We're all old geezers, but <i>you're</i> 
still tearing it up on the field.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:45.420
You two are also still out there, 
sweating with the Dolphins.

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:47.730
We're all real idiots here.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:48.920
You got that right.

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:53.850
Oh, that reminds me. You said you wanted a 
favor when you suggested coming for drinks.

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:54.930
What was it?

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:58.850
Oh, right. It's about Daigo.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:03.790
I wasn't around to see him play this season.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:07.440
I wondered if you could tell me 
all about his time with the Dolphins.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.540
Gimme all the details, no matter how small.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.190
So that means he's really 
done with baseball, huh?

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:15.780
Yeah...

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:19.530
Shigeno, what are you going to do?

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:21.700
Beats me.

00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:26.040
I haven't a clue, but whatever I decide 
to do, I have to give it my best shot.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.350
In baseball, I'm a veteran,

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:32.290
but as his dad, I'm a rookie.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.650
So?

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:40.780
Any bites?

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:41.600
Not one.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:43.950
What's up with you?

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:46.900
We agreed you'd take a day 
off from studying today.

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:48.870
I did, but...

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.500
Ha, look at 'em go.

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.360
Keep it up!

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:59.320
Thank you!

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:04.140
Pop, are you disappointed in me?

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:08.460
You wanted me to keep the baseball
tradition going, didn't you?

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:09.780
What are you talking about?

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:11.710
'Course I'm not disappointed in you.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:17.220
Are you saying that every kid of 
a baseball pro <i>has</i> to play baseball?

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.470
Daigo, you are your own man.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:22.300
Just do what you want to do.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.310
Actually, I...

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:26.220
Huh?

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:30.240
<i>I really wanted to show him.</i>

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:32.940
<i>I wanted to make Pop proud</i>

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:36.440
<i>by showing him how serious I was about 
baseball and how much progress I'd made.</i>

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:40.350
<i>But instead... But instead...</i>

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:46.790
Let's take a little detour.

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:50.500
This is...

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.380
Okay, let's go!

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.460
Mifune 
Batting Center

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:54.880
But I've already given up on...

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:59.420
I can't let myself get out of shape 
just because it's the off-season.

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:02.660
Go get a drink or something 
and hang around till I'm done.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.060
Fastballs

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.060
For both 
batting positions

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.060
Right-handed pitcher

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:13.660
It's been a while.

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:26.200
Wow!

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:30.160
Get a load of this guy!

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.820
I feel like I know him from somewhere...

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:36.020
Wait a minute. Can it be? 
It's that former major-leaguer—

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.770
Shigeno! It's Shigeno!

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:46.350
<i>Wow.</i>

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.890
<i>I remember what it felt 
like when I hit the ball.</i>

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:57.730
<i>Running like the wind,
 whatever kind of hit I got.</i>

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:21.140
Toshi, that you? I've got something 
important I want to talk to you about.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.830
Think we could meet up?

00:12:30.230 --> 00:12:32.020
What?

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:34.410
A family outing?

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.650
I don't have time for that!

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:38.650
I'm studying for my entrance exams!

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:42.330
It's fine! A day off will be 
a good change of pace for you.

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:44.830
And you're supposed to be studying, too, Sis!

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:47.230
I'm taking my textbook with me.

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:49.280
You're going that far?!

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:50.740
What's the big deal?

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:52.910
Having your pop here with us is rare enough.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:58.310
Not to mention, the reason he even planned 
this was because you're down in the dumps.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:00.420
Okay! Everything ready?

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.880
Let's go!

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.830
<i>This family is seriously messed up.</i>

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:11.270
<i>Since when do parents get in 
the way of studying for exams?!</i>

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:14.300
<i>Don't they care if I fail?</i>

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:30.270
Daigo.

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:32.140
Daigo!

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:34.830
We're here.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:45.190
What is... this place?

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:49.410
These last two months have 
been hard, haven't they, Daigo?

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:55.270
You might not believe this, but there were 
times when I wanted to quit baseball, too.

00:13:56.740 --> 00:13:59.120
Like when my pop died.

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:02.050
Or when I ruined my shoulder.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:03.280
Plenty of times.

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:04.990
<i>You</i> wanted to quit?

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:05.920
That's right.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:10.200
Which is why I'm not going to force 
you to play baseball against your will.

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:12.490
Baseball's supposed to be fun.

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:15.460
It's not meant to be about bad memories.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:21.070
If you love the game like I do,

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:23.930
I'm sure there will come a time
when you want to play again.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:29.480
It won't happen.

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:32.060
Not for me.

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:35.750
I'm not strong like you, Pop.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.640
I love baseball.

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:41.180
And I learned how fun playing catcher is.

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:45.220
How fun it is when the whole team 
pulls together as one to win a game.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:47.520
I was finally starting to <i>get</i> it!

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.760
And I actually <i>did</i> want to 
continue playing baseball.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:54.080
But...

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:59.950
I can't just keep on 
having fun playing baseball,

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:03.880
when I put my best friend, Hikaru,
 through something like that...

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:08.400
I can't do it.

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:14.100
Even if your friend forgives you?

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.790
H-Hikaru!

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.230
Hey. It's been a long time, Daigo-kun.

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:49.630
Are you surprised?

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:57.390
I'm really sorry I didn't tell you how much 
better I was feeling, Daigo-kun. I mean it.

00:15:58.130 --> 00:16:03.400
Truth is, I wanted to keep it a secret 
until I'd made a complete recovery.

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:08.710
But the other day, your 
father called up my papa.

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:12.670
I was shocked to hear that you 
blamed yourself for the accident,

00:16:12.670 --> 00:16:16.290
and that you were even talking 
about giving up baseball completely.

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:19.040
I'm sorry, Daigo-kun.

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:21.710
At the time, we didn't know 
how things would turn out.

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:25.820
But about two weeks after the accident,
he regained feeling in his upper body.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:31.550
Furutaka 
Rehabilitation 
Hospital

00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:31.550
And now, he's well enough to come to this 
rehabilitation center in a wheelchair.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:33.020
Rehabilitation?

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:38.110
Of course, I wanted to tell you 
right away so you could visit,

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:40.040
but Hikaru didn't want that.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:45.350
That's because I didn't want my best 
friend to see me looking so weak.

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:48.940
A-Aren't you mad at me, Hikaru?

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:51.440
Mad at you?

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:52.400
What for?

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.010
What do you mean, what for?

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:55.930
I ran into you and caused all this.

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:57.660
Of course I'm not mad.

00:16:58.180 --> 00:17:01.230
I'm the idiot who dived for 
the ball without calling for it.

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:02.410
It was all on me.

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:07.010
You had a much safer catch than I did.

00:17:07.010 --> 00:17:10.330
<i>I </i>was the one who got in <i>your</i> way 
and caused our team to lose.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:16.010
I felt so terrible about the whole thing,
I just couldn't face you guys.

00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:17.650
Hikaru...

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:26.950
B-But your legs...

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:33.260
With your legs out of action,
baseball isn't...

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:52.800
Daigo-kun.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:56.480
Go over to that wall.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.470
Here it comes, Daigo-kun!

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:15.280
And back, Daigo-kun.

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:30.620
Toshi, remember when my pop died?

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:32.500
Yeah, I remember.

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:38.880
Toshi-kun. Tomorrow... 
I'm moving to Mifune.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:42.800
Does that mean I can't play 
catch with you anymore?

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:44.620
I don't know.

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:48.190
But... my pop just died,

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:51.270
so I don't even want to watch,
 let alone play baseball.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:19:00.630
Goro-kun, wait!

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:08.910
Let me just catch one of 
your pitches, one last time!

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:12.880
Remember what I said to 
you in that letter before?

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:16.880
That one day, we'd become 
the strongest battery ever?

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.510
I may not be able to run yet,

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:26.010
but I'm going to join my middle school 
baseball team and make a comeback!

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:27.770
So...

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:34.800
You... can't quit baseball!

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:37.130
Even if we can't see each 
other anymore, I won't quit!

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:41.870
So you can't quit, either! You have to 
keep doing what your father taught you!

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:48.330
So, Daigo-kun, you can't quit 
the baseball you love, either!

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:04.520
Okay.

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:09.560
Wow, he is?!

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:11.210
That's great news!

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:12.250
Yeah!

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:14.590
Hey, wanna go to the batting cages?

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:16.400
Uh, sorry. Let's do that tomorrow.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:17.230
Huh?

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:22.490
I'm gonna break my baseball dry spell 
with a game of catch with my pop!

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:27.490
<i>Pop's gonna be so surprised.</i>

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:30.810
<i>I'll show him my super-framing catch!</i>

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.250
Shigeno

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:32.870
I'm home!

00:20:34.650 --> 00:20:37.620
Quick, Daigo! Run down to the 
station or you'll miss your pop!

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:38.960
Huh? What?

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:43.720
He said he's off to join the 
South American Winter League!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:47.730
Apparently, he didn't tell us because 
he didn't want us to talk him out of it!

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.410
<i>He can't be serious.</i>

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:56.800
<i>He just got home!</i>

00:20:56.800 --> 00:21:00.400
<i>How can that guy be so 
obsessed with baseball?!</i>

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:11.350
Pop!

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:20.140
Hey, Daigo!

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:21.000
What's up?

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:19.190
<i>Pop... I know I can never become you.</i>

00:22:20.620 --> 00:22:23.760
<i>But even so, I'm gonna get 
serious about baseball.</i>

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:04.750
Fuurin Academy Private Middle School

00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:07.140
Good. Next!

00:24:08.030 --> 00:24:12.310
I'm Sakura Mutsuko. In my last 
team, I played in the outfield.

00:24:13.170 --> 00:24:14.990
Good. Next!

00:24:15.720 --> 00:24:17.120
I'm Shigeno Daigo.

00:24:17.120 --> 00:24:18.950
I'm a catcher.

00:24:19.360 --> 00:24:20.790
It's nice to meet you!
